Subject: [PATCH] Measure the model seat in the provider's own unit; wire the
 two censuses

THE SEAT'S DAILY REQUEST ALLOWANCE IS THE DESK'S NOVEL-MECHANISM DISCOVERY RATE. A mechanism with
no registered family function reaches the gauntlet by one path only -- the compiler labels it
NEEDS_EXACT_RULE_EXTRACTION and a model call recovers the rule -- so the forests, the championship
records, the crawler and the arXiv feed all funnel through one account's daily allowance. Nothing
published that allowance, and what the desk believed about it was wrong.

MEASURED ON THIS BOX 2026-09-24, the provider's counter beside ours in one sitting:

  * THE ALLOWANCE WAS UNDERSTATED BY HALF, IN ITS OWN SOURCE. note_free_limit_hit recorded the
    desk's COMPLETION count at a 429 and called it "the ceiling"; the provider refuses in
    REQUESTS. 09-23: ours 460, theirs 1000. 09-24: ours 789, theirs 1008 of a 1000 limit. That
    460 reading became "the provider refused at 458 calls" in four docstrings and was read as the
    account's capacity. A budget in the wrong unit does not read as wrong -- it reads as a smaller
    desk. Both numbers are recorded now, each labelled with its unit, and provider_free_quota()
    asks /key for the authoritative {used, limit, remaining}.

  * THE GAP IS PURE WASTE AND NOBODY OWNED IT. 219 requests today and 540 on 09-23 produced no
    completion -- degradation retries, upstream 5xx, empty replies -- so 22% to 54% of the day's
    research budget bought nothing. It is the cheapest capacity on the desk: recovering it costs
    no money and needs no permission. LLM_BUDGET_CENSUS.json now names it hourly.

  * A FREE CALL BOOKED PHANTOM DOLLARS AND ARMED A LANDMINE ON THE UPGRADE PATH. _record_spend
    charged the over-estimate for :free models: $234.26 booked this month against a $20 cap and a
    true bill of zero. Nothing had failed only because free_tier_only() skips the cap check --
    which is the exact switch the principal flips to BUY capacity, and flipping it would have
    taken every organ dark inside one call with "monthly cap reached: $234.26 of $20.00". Free
    rows charge zero now, and month_spend_usd skips them BY MODEL ID so the append-only history
    cannot keep the cap tripped by its own past.

  * THE BUDGET HAD NO NAME ON IT. The ledger recorded the PROVIDER (openrouter) and never the
    CALLER, so "who drained the allowance by 01:42" could not be asked, let alone answered.
    calling_organ() stamps every row; the census names the largest consumer and its share.

  * TRUNCATION AND REFUSAL LOOKED IDENTICAL. 456 of 789 completed calls (58%) were discarded
    downstream as "reply was not a JSON object" -- and that parser already strips fences and scans
    brace-to-brace, so those replies carried no object at all. finish_reason, completion_tokens
    and reasoning_tokens are recorded per call now, which is the only way to tell a 700-token cap
    truncating a reasoning model from a model that would not answer. JSON_OBJECT and a
    response_format seam let a caller ask the provider to guarantee the shape; it degrades ahead
    of reasoning_effort, so a model without structured output never costs the caller its request.

  * EVERY 4xx LEAKED A TEMPORARY FILE. urllib's HTTPError is itself a response object; unclosed,
    it emits ResourceWarning from tempfile.__del__ at an arbitrary later moment, and under
    filterwarnings=error that failed whichever test the collector happened to interrupt --
    test_a_key_never_appears_in_full_in_a_report, whose own assertions pass. One leak per refusal
    on a rate-limited day. Closed.

  * THREE TESTS WERE READING THIS BOX'S LIVE STATE. test_llm_seat_free_tier never monkeypatched
    FREE_CEILING or SPEND_LEDGER, so it asserted against whatever the miners had done that day:
    green on a quiet build box, red here from the moment the 429 landed at 789 calls. The suite's
    colour tracked the time of day, which makes a real regression indistinguishable from a
    productive morning. An autouse fixture isolates them; all 80 seat tests now pass ON THIS BOX
    with the budget genuinely exhausted.

WIRED, because unwired is a defect (III.16) and both of these were built and left dark:

  * certificate_provenance was written, tested and NEVER RUN -- its artifact existed on neither
    box. Run here it finished in 89.5s and named all 174 certificates (111 ATTRIBUTED, 63
    FIRST_CLAIM, coverage 1.0), measuring that 19 of 548 producers have ever earned one. The
    desk's own capital-allocation question, answered in ninety seconds by code that had been
    complete and unscheduled. It is NOT a duplicate of attribution_census, already on this clock:
    that organ reaches coverage 1.0 through the symbol|family fallback certificate_provenance
    refuses by name, because 105-437 candidates share each pair across six or more producers, and
    a wrong producer misdirects compute as confidently as a right one.

  * llm_budget_census is new and publishes the above hourly, including whether the audit lane was
    starved: 7 recommendations raised in the last 7 days and 129 in 30, while the drain kept
    running and the seat was exhausted by 01:42 daily. That is an audit lane with no seat to call,
    not one with nothing to say.

Both enter issue_board.CADENCE at 3600s, so MT5-ResearchReports (hourly, SYSTEM) runs them and the
issue board notices either going quiet. No gate, cap or threshold is changed and nothing is
rationed; fixed_trial_count is untouched. First census on this box: provider used 1008/1000,
desk 789 completions, 219 invisible, 15 of 15 seats pinned.

